---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { ANALYTICS, usesAnalytics, usesGoogleAnalytics } from '../config/analytics';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Zo Media Productions collects, uses, and protects information from visitors, subscribers, and supporters."
  updated="October 6, 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE.legalName} ("Zo Media," "we," "us") is a media cooperative and a subsidiary of the
    {SITE.parent.name} ({SITE.parent.shortName}), {SITE.parent.note}. This policy explains what information we collect through
    zomediaproductions.com, how we use it, and the choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Messages you send us.</strong> When you use the contact form we receive your name, email address, optional organization, inquiry type, subject, and message.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter signups.</strong> When you subscribe to updates or The Phuckin' Wire we receive your email address and which page you signed up from.</li>
    <li><strong>Donations.</strong> Donations are processed by our donation platform (Give Lively), not on this site. We never receive or store your card or bank details. The platform shares donor name, email, and gift details with the nonprofit so we can issue receipts and thank you.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical information.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider automatically logs your IP address, browser type, device, and the pages requested. {usesAnalytics ? 'We also use website analytics to understand which pages are useful (see "Analytics" below).' : 'If we enable website analytics, we will use it to understand which pages are useful, and we will update this policy.'}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your messages and run our programs.</li>
    <li>To send the updates you asked for. You can unsubscribe from any email at any time.</li>
    <li>To issue donation receipts and meet nonprofit record-keeping obligations.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure, prevent spam and abuse, and fix problems.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for advertising profiles.</p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on trusted providers to operate the site: web hosting and form handling, email delivery, newsletter delivery,
    and donation processing. They may process your information only to provide their services to us and under their own
    privacy and security commitments.
  </p>

  {usesAnalytics && (
    <>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      {usesGoogleAnalytics ? (
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to measure how the site is used (pages viewed, devices, approximate location). It sets
          cookies in your browser. We have turned off advertising features and Google signals. You can opt out with
          the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a> or your browser's privacy settings.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          We use privacy-friendly analytics ({ANALYTICS.plausibleDomain}) that counts visits in aggregate without cookies
          or personal profiles.
        </p>
      )}
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    {usesGoogleAnalytics
      ? 'Apart from analytics cookies described above, this site does not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.'
      : 'This site does not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.'}
    Third-party tools we embed (for example, the donation form) may set their own cookies needed for them to work; see
    their privacy policies for details.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep messages for as long as needed to respond and to keep reasonable records of our work. We keep newsletter
    addresses until you unsubscribe. Donation records are kept as required for nonprofit and tax purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you, or stop emailing you, by
    writing to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Depending on where you live (for example, California),
    you may have additional rights under local law, and we will honor valid requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS and we limit access to the information we collect. No method of transmission or
    storage is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We will post any changes on this page and update the date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.legalName}<br />
    {SITE.address.streetAddress}, {SITE.address.addressLocality}, {SITE.address.addressRegion} {SITE.address.postalCode}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> &middot; <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
